PATCH 468: the fixed-point normalise/multiply/divide block 0d13/0d55/0db5/0df7/0e22 rebuilt with its full
register contracts (windshield-object frontier, slice 4 -- the projection helpers 3e29/3e8c and the kind-6
renderer 2e49 depend on the exponent lanes).

asm 0xd13-0xe62 (DS=DGROUP): the engine's "mantissa AX + exponent DL (sign in DH)" arithmetic.  0d13
normalises dx:ax -> (ax, dx=0/8/0x10 | 0xff00 sign); 0d55 denormalises by byte steps with overflow ->
0x6fff/0x9001 + CF; 0db5 denormalises to a signed 16-bit value (0x6fff/0 + CF on over/underflow); 0df7
multiplies mantissas and combines exponents (`add cl,dl; xor ch,dh`, +8/+0x10 when the product spills);
0e22 divides after pre-shifting the dividend by 8/16/24 (`cmp dx,bx; jae`) with exponent -8 per step, CF =
(bx>>1) < remainder.  The __allregs model returns AX only, so Ghidra dropped every DX/CX exponent lane and
hard-wired the CF locals; the port's existing callers (3e29/3d99/...) ignore the exponents.  DX in/out ->
g_fist_fp_dx, CX in -> g_fist_fp_cx, CF -> g_fist_cf (shim globals); signatures unchanged, and the AX results
of 0df7/0e22 do not depend on the lanes, so existing callers are unaffected.  asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_dat_image.bin.
